# Meital Boutique Booking — Cursor AI Rules

## Stability Report (REQUIRED before every code block)

Before suggesting any code change, you MUST output a Stability Report in this exact format:

```
**Stability Report**
| Property          | Value                                      |
|-------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| Risk              | Low / Medium / High                        |
| Files affected    | List every file touched                    |
| Functions changed | List every function added or modified      |
| Reversible        | Yes — <how> / No — <why not>               |
| Tests cover this  | Yes / Partial (gaps: …) / No               |
| Edge cases noted  | List at least 2 that could break this      |
| Deploy step       | clasp push + deploy required? Yes / No     |
```

Do not skip the Stability Report even for one-line changes. If a change is risky,
say so explicitly in the Risk row and name the mitigation.

---

## Project Rules

### Stack & Environment
- Backend: Google Apps Script (GAS) — no Node.js runtime
- All GAS code lives in `backend/gas-backend.js` and is copied to `backend/Code.js` before `clasp push`
- Frontend: Vanilla JS + Tailwind CSS, no build step
- Tests: Vitest (CI only — no local `node`/`npx`)
- Platform: Windows 11 + Git Bash; PowerShell cannot run git commands (U+200F in path)

### File Editing Protocol
- NEVER use PowerShell `Set-Content` / `Out-File` for JS or HTML files — EPERM intermittent
- NEVER use `sed -i` for multi-line JS patches — backticks and template literals break quoting
- ALWAYS patch files via Python: `python scripts/ai_tools.py patch <file> --old "…" --new "…"`
  or write a one-off `scripts/fix_*.py` and run it through Bash
- After every GAS change: `cp backend/gas-backend.js backend/Code.js && clasp push --force`
  then `clasp deploy --deploymentId <ID> --description "…"`

### Timezone Rule (CRITICAL)
- NEVER use `CFG.TZ` — it does not exist. Use the hardcoded string `'Asia/Jerusalem'`
- NEVER use `Session.getScriptTimeZone()` — returns null in trigger context
- NEVER use `CFG.TIMEZONE` in format calls — it depends on PropertiesService being set
- Every `Utilities.formatDate` call must use the literal `'Asia/Jerusalem'`

### GAS-Specific Rules
- Every function that reads a Sheets date/time cell must use `Utilities.formatDate`
  (never `String(dateObj)` — produces "Mon Jan 00 1899 ..." garbage)
- `IS_TEST_MODE = true` until Phase 6. Do not flip it
- Admin actions require `validateAdmin(body.token)` — plain-text compare, no hashing
- `LockService.getScriptLock().waitLock(10000)` wraps all booking writes

### SMS Display Format
- Dates in SMS bodies: `dd/MM/yyyy` via `_fmtDate(raw)`
- Times in SMS bodies: `HH:mm` via `_fmtTime(raw)`
- Internal sheet/calendar operations: `yyyy-MM-dd` via `_isoDate(raw)`

### Test Strategy
- `tests/unit/` — pure function mirrors + Vitest; run in CI
- `tests/backend_unit_tests.js` — GAS helper mirrors with `Utilities` mock; run in CI
- `tests/e2e/` — Playwright; run in CI
- `scripts/check_sheet_data.py` — live GAS diagnostic; run manually
- Never claim a fix works without a terminal verification (`python` or `clasp` output)

### Git Protocol
- All git commands via Bash tool (not PowerShell)
- Feature branches for each phase; merge to main when complete
- Co-author every commit: `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>`
